course: dictionary
lesson: 14636
title: Praising effort and good deeds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell us that something deserves to be admired. Praiseworthy is one of them. Its clues are often in the sentence around it. «Sam shared his lunch with a new girl who had none. That was praiseworthy.» Sharing with someone who has nothing is kind and good, so praiseworthy must mean deserving praise.
explain: Look for words like «but» that show a contrast. «Our team lost the match, but Ella's effort was praiseworthy.» The word «but» tells you the team did not win, yet we still admire something. So praiseworthy can mean worth praising even when the result is not perfect.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «worth praising» in place of praiseworthy. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is probably right. The word often praises a person's effort or aim, not only what they achieved.
fact: Praiseworthy means deserving praise; good and admirable.
fact: Praiseworthy can also mean worth approving of, even if the person was not completely successful.
fact: «A praiseworthy effort» means someone tried hard, even if the result was not perfect.
fact: Praiseworthy is a slightly formal word, so you will often see it in school reports and in stories about good behaviour.
exercise: «Sam shared his lunch with a new girl who had none. That was praiseworthy.» What does praiseworthy mean here? | Hard to see | Silly and funny | Very loud | *Good and deserving praise
exercise: «Our team lost the match, but Ella's effort in every game was praiseworthy.» What is the praise for? | The weather | The referee's whistle | The score | *The effort, even though they lost
exercise: Which word means about the same as praiseworthy? | Careless | Noisy | Sleepy | *Admirable
test: «Priya finished her sums neatly, even though they were hard. Her work is praiseworthy.» What does praiseworthy mean in this sentence? | Easy to lose | Needs to be thrown away | Very expensive | *Deserves praise
test: Mr Hale wrote: «Jack's praiseworthy aim is to help younger children read.» What does praiseworthy show about Jack's aim? | It is finished | It is rude | It is secret | *It is good and worth admiring
exam: «Ben's praiseworthy effort in the test showed how hard he worked, even though he did not pass.» What does this suggest about praiseworthy? | Means he failed completely | Shows Ben cheated | *Worth praising even without full success | Means he was lucky
